verdicts.gain_estimate:
K per response dm is 4-5x faster on caffeine/SVP and about 8-10x on TZVP. Whole runs:
- benzene DF-B3LYP TDA: about -22%, as measured;
- caffeine/SVP DF-B3LYP TDA: XC about 18 s plus DF-K 17-31 s drops to XC plus 5-9 s, about 1.45-1.75x overall (slightly below the analyst's 1.5-2x upper end);
- DF hybrid Hessian CPHF K: about 3.5-4x;
- the dsyrk change in the SCF MO branch saves 25% of DF-SCF K flops (only hybrid DF SCF; DF-PBE has no K).

RKS:
- caffeine B3LYP Hessian: about -1 to -1.5 s (0.6-0.8%);
- caffeine TDA: at most -0.4 s (1.6%).
UKS (unprofiled, scaled from the per-set cost):
- caffeine+ UKS TDA: about -1.3 to -2.2 s of about 50 s (2.5-4%);
- UKS GGA Hessian: about -3 to -6 s (1-2%);
- UKS MGGA Hessian: about -5 to -9 s (1.5-2.5%).
